Using Field + NumberField and a `validate` function:
1. the input is initially empty `<NumberField.Root defaultValue={undefined} />`
2. type a number then blur/tab away, the validate function is called with `null` as the value instead of the textbox's value
3. refocus the input and blur again, it gets called with the latest (correct) value

Sandbox: https://codesandbox.io/p/sandbox/vibrant-sanderson-m78kcl

```jsx
<Field.Root
  name="amount"
  validationMode="onBlur"
  validate={(value) => {
    console.log("validate", value);
    if (value === undefined || value == null || value === 0) {
      return 'Amount is required';
    }
    if (typeof value === "number" && Number.isFinite(value)) {
      if (value > 50) {
        return 'Insufficient balance, your remaining balance is 50.00';
      }
      if (value < 20) {
        return 'The minimum amount is 20.00';
      }
    }
    return null;
  }}
>
  <NumberField.Root required defaultValue={undefined}>
    <Field.Label>Transfer Amount</Field.Label>
    <NumberField.Input placeholder="Amount in SGD" />
  </NumberField.Root>
  <Field.Error match="customError" />
</Field.Root>
```
